My mother asks if I was okay that first evening.
The apartment was furnished, but completely strange.
I had no food in the kitchen yet.
I bought a simple dinner on the way home.
It was just a sandwich in a paper bag.
I sat alone on the little sofa.
The apartment was very quiet.
I ate my food all alone.
I did not know anyone in the city yet.
"I missed you all a lot that evening," I say to her.
I thought about my sister Sofía and my brother Diego.
I even missed our dog Lola.
I felt lonely.
My mother smiles warmly at me through the screen.
"The beginning is always difficult," she replies.
I nod and think back to the day.
It was a difficult evening, but the next morning was much better.
